1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,270
One morning, everyone you know has a

2
00:00:02,290 --> 00:00:03,934
number over their head.

3
00:00:03,954 --> 00:00:05,075
Your barista.

4
00:00:05,095 --> 00:00:06,840
Two thousand and ninety.

5
00:00:06,860 --> 00:00:07,845
Your boss.

6
00:00:07,865 --> 00:00:09,485
Four hundred and twelve.

7
00:00:09,505 --> 00:00:10,767
Your best friend.

8
00:00:11,407 --> 00:00:12,253
Three.

9
00:00:12,843 --> 00:00:14,248
It doesn't say why.

10
00:00:14,268 --> 00:00:15,996
It only says how long.

11
00:00:19,046 --> 00:00:20,651
You don't know what it's counting.

12
00:00:20,671 --> 00:00:21,541
Not yet.

13
00:00:21,561 --> 00:00:23,192
Your neighbour's says zero.

14
00:00:23,212 --> 00:00:23,617
Morning!

15
00:00:23,637 --> 00:00:23,892
Well.

16
00:00:23,912 --> 00:00:24,817
Last morning.

17
00:00:24,837 --> 00:00:25,601
Van's here.

18
00:00:25,621 --> 00:00:26,606
You're moving?

19
00:00:26,626 --> 00:00:27,606
To the coast!

20
00:00:27,626 --> 00:00:28,887
Did I not tell you?

21
00:00:29,037 --> 00:00:29,787
Zero.

22
00:00:29,827 --> 00:00:30,697
And he's gone.

23
00:00:30,717 --> 00:00:32,172
So that's what it counts.

24
00:00:32,192 --> 00:00:32,897
Days.

25
00:00:32,917 --> 00:00:34,685
Until someone leaves your life.

26
00:00:36,495 --> 00:00:37,292
Usual?

27
00:00:37,312 --> 00:00:38,873
You're going to be here a while.

28
00:00:38,893 --> 00:00:39,682
Thanks?

29
00:00:40,732 --> 00:00:42,602
At work, you check everyone.

30
00:00:42,622 --> 00:00:44,711
Your boss, four hundred and twelve.

31
00:00:44,731 --> 00:00:45,897
You do the maths.

32
00:00:45,917 --> 00:00:47,447
A promotion, probably.

33
00:00:47,467 --> 00:00:48,087
His.

34
00:00:48,107 --> 00:00:49,072
Your colleague.

35
00:00:49,092 --> 00:00:49,865
Twelve.

36
00:00:49,885 --> 00:00:50,870
You're quitting.

37
00:00:50,890 --> 00:00:51,490
What?

38
00:00:51,530 --> 00:00:54,689
Who told I haven't even told my mum.

39
00:00:54,839 --> 00:00:55,969
The office plant.

40
00:00:55,989 --> 00:00:56,469
Four.

41
00:00:56,489 --> 00:00:57,984
Nobody's watering it.

42
00:00:58,004 --> 00:00:59,434
Your gym says zero.

43
00:00:59,454 --> 00:01:00,279
Fair.

44
00:01:00,633 --> 00:01:02,583
But you keep coming back to three.

45
00:01:04,233 --> 00:01:05,199
You're staring.

46
00:01:05,219 --> 00:01:05,699
Am I?

47
00:01:05,719 --> 00:01:06,990
Your hair looks nice.

48
00:01:07,010 --> 00:01:08,293
It's the same hair.

49
00:01:08,443 --> 00:01:09,418
Three days.

50
00:01:09,438 --> 00:01:11,168
So you do what anyone would.

51
00:01:11,188 --> 00:01:13,681
You make yourself impossible to leave.

52
00:01:13,701 --> 00:01:15,106
Her favourite coffee.

53
00:01:15,126 --> 00:01:16,301
Every morning.

54
00:01:16,321 --> 00:01:18,616
The shelf she asked about in March.

55
00:01:18,636 --> 00:01:20,416
The story about her cousin.

56
00:01:20,436 --> 00:01:21,941
You laugh at all of it.

57
00:01:21,961 --> 00:01:22,799
Again.

58
00:01:22,819 --> 00:01:23,494
Okay.

59
00:01:23,514 --> 00:01:24,938
Who are you, and what do you want?

60
00:01:24,958 --> 00:01:25,633
Nothing!

61
00:01:25,653 --> 00:01:27,325
Can't a friend fix a shelf?

62
00:01:27,875 --> 00:01:29,050
That night, you check.

63
00:01:29,417 --> 00:01:30,247
Two.

64
00:01:31,157 --> 00:01:31,717
Hey.

65
00:01:31,737 --> 00:01:32,977
Can I tell you something?

66
00:01:32,997 --> 00:01:34,112
First, dessert!

67
00:01:34,132 --> 00:01:35,527
I got the one you like.

68
00:01:35,927 --> 00:01:36,687
Sure.

69
00:01:36,837 --> 00:01:38,712
She was about to say something.

70
00:01:38,732 --> 00:01:40,627
You gave her cake instead.

71
00:01:40,647 --> 00:01:42,687
It isn't counting how she feels.

72
00:01:42,707 --> 00:01:44,096
It's just counting.

73
00:01:45,086 --> 00:01:46,541
So you start guessing.

74
00:01:46,561 --> 00:01:48,166
A fight you haven't had yet.

75
00:01:48,186 --> 00:01:49,766
Something a doctor said.

76
00:01:49,786 --> 00:01:51,106
Something you said.

77
00:01:51,126 --> 00:01:52,880
You read every message you've sent her

78
00:01:52,900 --> 00:01:53,910
since spring.

79
00:01:54,501 --> 00:01:55,279
One.

80
00:01:57,229 --> 00:01:59,156
You find out by accident.

81
00:01:59,176 --> 00:01:59,796
Mira.

82
00:01:59,816 --> 00:02:00,844
What's all this?

83
00:02:00,864 --> 00:02:01,539
Okay.

84
00:02:01,559 --> 00:02:02,401
Don't be mad.

85
00:02:02,421 --> 00:02:03,161
I got in.

86
00:02:03,181 --> 00:02:03,986
The course.

87
00:02:04,006 --> 00:02:05,495
The one that said no last year.

88
00:02:05,515 --> 00:02:07,017
Mira, that's huge!

89
00:02:07,037 --> 00:02:08,317
It's four hours away.

90
00:02:08,337 --> 00:02:09,487
It starts Monday.

91
00:02:09,887 --> 00:02:11,214
And you didn't tell me.

92
00:02:11,234 --> 00:02:12,074
I tried!

93
00:02:12,094 --> 00:02:13,439
Like, nine times.

94
00:02:13,459 --> 00:02:15,089
But you were being so nice.

95
00:02:15,109 --> 00:02:16,819
And I thought, if I tell him, he'll

96
00:02:16,839 --> 00:02:18,244
be nice about that too.

97
00:02:18,264 --> 00:02:20,136
And I'll never know what he really thinks.

98
00:02:20,636 --> 00:02:21,591
I think…

99
00:02:21,741 --> 00:02:23,096
Her number flickers.

100
00:02:23,116 --> 00:02:23,471
One.

101
00:02:23,491 --> 00:02:24,196
Nine hundred.

102
00:02:24,216 --> 00:02:24,786
One.

103
00:02:24,806 --> 00:02:26,690
If you ask her now, she stays.

104
00:02:27,600 --> 00:02:29,588
I think you're going to need more tape.

105
00:02:29,608 --> 00:02:30,690
That's what you think?

106
00:02:30,710 --> 00:02:33,035
And I think I'm going to hate Mondays.

107
00:02:34,335 --> 00:02:36,065
Why are you wrapping one mug in three

108
00:02:36,085 --> 00:02:36,722
jumpers?

109
00:02:36,742 --> 00:02:38,281
It's your favourite mug.

110
00:02:38,301 --> 00:02:39,126
It's your mug.

111
00:02:39,146 --> 00:02:40,245
I stole it in March.

112
00:02:40,265 --> 00:02:41,860
Then it's coming with you.

113
00:02:42,510 --> 00:02:44,540
You carry the heavy box.

114
00:02:44,560 --> 00:02:46,415
She pretends not to notice you picked

115
00:02:46,435 --> 00:02:47,409
the heavy one.

116
00:02:48,399 --> 00:02:50,507
Zero is a train platform.

117
00:02:50,527 --> 00:02:51,632
Don't make it weird.

118
00:02:51,652 --> 00:02:53,234
I'm not making it weird.

119
00:02:53,254 --> 00:02:54,356
You're doing the face.

120
00:02:54,376 --> 00:02:55,898
Text me when you get there.

121
00:02:55,918 --> 00:02:56,993
It's four hours.

122
00:02:57,033 --> 00:02:57,840
Not the moon.

123
00:02:57,860 --> 00:02:59,523
Then text me from the moon.

124
00:03:00,473 --> 00:03:01,828
The doors close.

125
00:03:01,848 --> 00:03:03,779
The number goes out like a light.

126
00:03:05,689 --> 00:03:06,629
Seat fourteen.

127
00:03:06,649 --> 00:03:07,564
Already bored.

128
00:03:07,584 --> 00:03:08,608
Call you tonight?

129
00:03:09,258 --> 00:03:11,288
There's no number over her name.

130
00:03:11,308 --> 00:03:13,363
It was never counting the friendship.

131
00:03:13,383 --> 00:03:14,736
Only the distance.

132
00:03:17,126 --> 00:03:18,978
Would you have asked her to stay?
